.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-I\fP, \fB\-\-input\fP \fIgrid\fP
Input grid file. Required.
.TP
.B \-O\fP, \fB\-\-output\fP \fIroot\fP
Output root name. Default: the input grid's basename with its
extension removed.
.TP
.B \-\-format \fIfmt\fP
Output format passed to \fBgmt figure\fP. Default \fBpdf\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-title \fItext\fP
Plot title.
.TP
.B \-\-colorbar\-label \fItext\fP
Label for the color scale bar. Default \fBz\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-dpi \fIdpi\fP
Rendering resolution: both \fBgrdview\fP's own \fB\-Qi\fP\fIdpi\fP
(\fB\-\-color\-mode\fP 1-5 only) and the final raster's resolution.
.TP
.B \-X\fP, \fB\-\-execute
Run the generated script immediately after writing it.
.TP
.B \-V\fP, \fB\-\-verbose
Print the generated script's path and a one-line summary.
.TP
.B \-R\fP, \fB\-\-region \fIxmin/xmax/ymin/ymax\fP
Plot region. Default: the grid's own bounds.
.TP
.B \-J\fP, \fB\-\-projection \fIspec\fP
GMT map projection/scale spec. Default: an auto-fit Mercator
(geographic grids) or linear (all others) projection chosen to fill
the page, adjusted for the chosen \fB\-\-view\fP azimuth's apparent
footprint.
.TP
.B \-P\fP, \fB\-\-pagesize \fIsize\fP
Page size code. Default \fBa\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-portrait\fP, \fB\-\-landscape
Force the page orientation instead of choosing automatically.
.TP
.B \-\-scale\-location \fI{l,r,t,b}\fP
Color scale bar placement. Default \fBb\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-tick\-info \fIspec\fP
Raw \fB\-B\fP basemap tick-interval spec (covering x, y, and z axes
together), overriding the automatically computed one.
.TP
.B \-\-length\-scale \fIspec\fP
A GMT distance (map) scale bar spec, passed as \fB\-L\fP\fIspec\fP on
\fBgmt basemap\fP.
.TP
.B \-E\fP, \fB\-\-view \fIazimuth/elevation\fP
Viewpoint azimuth/elevation of the 3D perspective, e.g. \fB150/15\fP.
Default \fB240/30\fP. Also determines which two of the four vertical
frame walls are drawn/annotated.
.TP
.B \-F\fP, \fB\-\-exaggeration \fIfactor\fP
Vertical exaggeration. If neither this nor \fB\-\-zscale\fP is given,
the map z-scale defaults to \fB2.0/(zmax\-zmin)\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-zscale \fIval\fP
Explicit map z-scale (\fB\-Jz\fP\fIval\fP), overriding
\fB\-\-exaggeration\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-color\-mode \fI{1-7}\fP
1 plain color fill; 2 color shaded relief; 3 color shaded by a supplied
intensity grid; 4 color fill of slope magnitude; 5 color shaded by
slope magnitude; 6 wireframe mesh plot (no color fill); 7 wireframe
mesh plot with contour lines (see the GMT-bug note above). Default 1.
.TP
.B \-W\fP, \fB\-\-color\-control \fIspec\fP
Either \fIstyle\fP[\fB/\fP\fIpalette\fP[\fB/\fP\fIncolors\fP]], or the
path to an existing \fB.cpt\fP file to use as-is.
.TP
.B \-D\fP, \fB\-\-color\-flip
Reverse the color palette.
.TP
.B \-Y\fP, \fB\-\-no\-nice\-interval
Use a direct linear color stretch instead of a rounded interval.
.TP
.B \-\-stretch\-color
Histogram-equalize the color stretch (\fB\-\-color\-mode\fP 1 only).
.TP
.B \-Z\fP, \fB\-\-zbounds \fIzmin/zmax\fP
Override the grid's own detected z-range, affecting the color stretch,
the vertical axis, and the z-scale/exaggeration calculation.
.TP
.B \-\-data\-scale \fIfactor\fP
Rescale grid values by \fIfactor\fP before colorizing/shading.
.TP
.B \-\-magnitude \fIval\fP, \fB\-\-azimuth \fIdeg\fP, \fB\-\-elevation \fIdeg\fP
Illumination/slope-shading parameters for \fB\-\-color\-mode\fP 2-5
(the sun's azimuth/elevation for synthetic illumination, distinct from
\fB\-\-view\fP's viewpoint azimuth/elevation).
.TP
.B \-\-shade\-flip
Reverse the shading direction (negates the effective magnitude).
.TP
.B \-\-intensity\-file \fIgrid\fP
Intensity grid for \fB\-\-color\-mode\fP 3.
.TP
.B \-\-stretch\-shade
Histogram-equalize the intensity file first (\fB\-\-color\-mode\fP 3 only).
.TP
.B \-\-mesh\-contour\-pen \fIpen\fP
Draw contour lines directly on the mesh (\fB\-\-color\-mode\fP 7 only).
See the GMT-bug note above.
.TP
.B \-\-drape\-file \fIgrid\fP
A grid to drape on the relief (\fBgrdview\fP's \fB\-G\fP) instead of
coloring the surface directly from the CPT.
.TP
.B \-\-mesh\-null \fI[level/r/g/b]\fP
Null-plane level/color for undefined (NaN) nodes (\fBgrdview\fP's
\fB\-N\fP). If given with no value, defaults to
\fI<zmin>\fP\fB/200/200/200\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-mesh\-zlevel \fIval\fP
Z level for the base plane and frame (\fBgrdview\fP's and
\fBgmt basemap\fP's \fB\-Z\fP).
.TP
.B \-\-coast
Enable a coastline overlay (\fBgmt coast\fP), projected into the same
3D perspective.
.TP
.B \-\-coast\-resolution \fI{f,h,i,l,c}\fP
Coastline database resolution: full, high, intermediate, low, crude.
.TP
.B \-\-coast\-dry\-fill\fP, \fB\-\-coast\-wet\-fill\fP, \fB\-\-coast\-lake\-fill \fIcolor\fP
Fill colors for land, water, and lakes.
.TP
.B \-\-coast\-river \fIcolor\fP
Draw rivers in the given color.
.TP
.B \-\-coast\-boundary \fIspec\fP
Draw a national boundary; repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-coast\-pen \fIpen\fP
Pen for the coastline itself.
.TP
.B \-\-text \fIlon/lat/size/angle/font/justify/text\fP
Place a text label (\fBgmt text\fP), projected into the 3D view.
Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-gmt\-default \fIparam/value\fP
Override a GMT default parameter for this plot; repeatable.

.SH EXAMPLES
A shaded-relief 3D perspective view, viewed from azimuth 150, elevation
15 degrees, rendered directly to a 300 dpi PNG:

.br
 mbpy_grd3dplot \-I topo.grd \-O topo3d \\
.br
     \-\-color\-mode 2 \-\-magnitude 0.2 \-\-azimuth 90 \-\-elevation 5 \\
.br
     \-\-view 150/15 \\
.br
     \-\-title "Survey Area" \-\-colorbar\-label "Topography (meters)" \\
.br
     \-\-length\-scale "fx10/2/32.70/5.0+lkm" \\
.br
     \-\-pagesize c \-\-dpi 300 \-\-format png \-\-execute \-V

A plain wireframe mesh view:

.br
 mbpy_grd3dplot \-I topo.grd \-O topomesh \\
.br
     \-\-color\-mode 6 \-\-view 210/25 \-\-title "Survey Area" \\
.br
     \-\-format png \-\-execute \-V

